  "details": "nginx is a web and proxy server supporting HTTP and other protocols, with a focus on high concurrency, performance, and low memory usage.   \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * nginx: NGINX flow control window overflow in HTTP/2 (CVE-2026-123007)\n  * nginx: NGINX use-after-free condition in the resolver (CVE-2026-123634)\n  * nginx: NGINX use-after-free in worker process when using HTTP/2 (CVE-2026-123633)\n  * nginx: NGINX use-after-free in worker process in the mail proxy server (CVE-2026-113425)\n  * nginx: nginx: Denial of Service via crafted TLS connection (CVE-2026-118899)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
